TITLE:: VSTPluginBrowser
summary:: a VST plugin browser dialog
categories:: GUI
related:: Classes/VSTPlugin, Classes/VSTPluginController, Classes/VSTPluginDesc, Classes/VSTPluginGui

DESCRIPTION::
This class creates a dialog window where you can browse already loaded plugins, start a new search in the default directories
(see link::Classes/VSTPlugin#*search::) or load a plugin from a file dialog.

IMAGE::browser.jpg::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

ARGUMENT:: mode
This must be one the following Symbols:

definitionlist::
## code::\dialog:: ||
The browser imitates the behavior of a modal dialog window: the window always stays on top and it is automatically closed when the user clicks the "Open" button. (The window is not truely modal, though, because the user can still interact with other SC GUI windows.)

## code::\normal:: ||
The browser behaves like a regular window. If you click the "Open" button, the action function is called but the window stays open.

## code::\browse:: ||
You can browse and search for plugins, but there are no controls for opening a plugin.
::

ARGUMENT:: server
the Server that is used for searching plugins. If code::nil::, the default Server is assumed.

DISCUSSION::
Typically, you do not create a VSTPluginBrowser yourself. Instead, it is created automatically when you call link::Classes/VSTPluginController#-browse:: or when you press the "Browse" button in link::Classes/VSTPluginGui::.

However, if you create the instance manually, you have more control over the appearance because you have direct access to all the link::Classes/Window:: methods:

code::
b = VSTPluginBrowser(\normal);
// do not destroy on close
b.deleteOnClose = false;
// attach custom action
b.action = { |info, options| "received % with options %".format(info, options).postln };
// show
b.front;
// close programmatically
b.close;
// show again
b.front;
// really close and destroy
b.destroy;
::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: initBrowser, prSearchDir, prApplyFilter, prBuildGui, prUpdatePlugins, prSearchRunning, prSetCurrentPlugin, prPluginSelected, prSearch, prOpenFile, prClear, prOpen

METHOD:: action
Attach a custom action.

If the user clicks the "Open" button, the action will be called with the selected link::Classes/VSTPluginDesc:: and an link::Classes/Event:: with options that can be passed to link::Classes/VSTPluginController#-open::.

If the user clicks the "Cancel" button, the action will receive code::nil:: instead.

In SC 3.14 and above you can simply pass the options as

METHOD:: deleteOnClose
Sets or gets whether the window should be destroyed when closed.

METHOD:: destroy
Close and destroy the window regardless the link::#-deleteOnClose:: propertiy.

METHOD:: currentPlugin
Sets or gets the currently selected plugin.
